Subject: [PATCH 01235/11171] [conductor] In-process docs for HIERARCHICAL
 SEARCH OVER THE VERIFIED vc33 WORLD MODEL (the G2 DEPTH TEST -- is the .372
 search layer a general planner or an r11l trick?): build a planning search
 over the vc33 verified WM (reuse exp4034's goal predicate + the saved WM
 program as the forward simulator) with (a) SUBGOAL/LANDMARK decomposition
 (HWM arXiv:2604.03208 / Subgoal-PHS arXiv:2506.07255 -- the lever for
 long-horizon where flat search blows up), (b) a NON-bespoke coded heuristic
 over the goal predicate (unmet goal components / manhattan-to-target /
 progress-delta -- NOT game-specific hardcoded macros like exp4021's
 r11l_safe_composite_path_macro), (c) a REAL bounded best-first/A* search
 (report nodes_expanded + branching honestly -- exp4021 expanded only 3).
 REAL-ENV-CONFIRM any solve via level_completed. Honest no-solve is a COMPLETE
 verdict. The diagnostic: did the search break vc33's wall (where the 99%-WM
 single-step approach failed), and did it do so with a GENERAL heuristic or
 did it need vc33-specific macros?

